WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.500
SCP-682 Vs a Vacuum.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.210
And we’re not talking about the household
cleaning appliance.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:10.020
Could the Hard to Destroy Reptile survive
in a completely air-free environment?

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:15.650
To find out, 99% of the oxygen was removed
from a testing chamber that SCP-682 was trapped

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.650
inside.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.300
The creature entered a dormant state, and
began producing what the Foundation believed

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:27.670
to be its native atmosphere - A mixture of
56% ozone, 23% chlorine, 18% xenon, and other

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.140
caustic elements.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.540
The test was eventually called to an end,
however, when our normal earth atmosphere

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:37.550
was reintroduced into the room, it reacted
with the compound that 682 was releasing,

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.650
and caused a massive explosion that blew off
the blast door.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:45.740
A scientist remarked that it was no wonder
682 was so hardy if that poisonous mix was

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.210
its native atmosphere.

